Third-party components
======================

vendor/primus-core — Primus zkTLS core (LGPL-3.0)
--------------------------------------------------

`vendor/primus-core` is a git submodule reference to

    https://github.com/OpenKaito/primus-extension-fork

a fork of Primus Labs' browser extension
(https://github.com/primus-labs/primus-extension). That project is distributed
under the **GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3**; see
`vendor/primus-core/LICENSE` after initialising the submodule.

The fork's package metadata directs readers to the `LICENSE` file. This
repository treats that LGPL-3.0 file as governing the Primus portion.

What this repository contains, and what it distributes, are two different
things, and both matter:

  * This REPOSITORY contains no part of that project's source. It carries a
    gitlink — a commit id — plus the `.gitmodules` entry that resolves it.
    `git submodule update --init` fetches the code from the URL above at build
    time. Kaito-authored files in this repository are under the proprietary licence in `LICENSE`.

  * The BUILT EXTENSION is a combined work. It includes the LGPL-3.0 code from
    that fork alongside Kaito-authored proprietary code, and `modules/primus.ts`
    modifies that component's build output while assembling it. Anyone
    distributing a built artifact is distributing that combined work and carries
    the LGPL's obligations for the Primus portion.

How those obligations are discharged, and where each part lives:

  * **Complete corresponding source, at the exact built revision.** The gitlink
    pins one commit of the fork above; `git submodule status` prints it. The
    pinned fork tracks the `pnpm-lock.yaml` consumed by the parent build, and
    vendor installation uses `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`.
    `.gitmodules` also sets `shallow = true`, and a fork can be force-pushed, so
    the commit is written as a literal into every release artifact (see below).

  * **Licence texts, inside the distributed artifact.** A NOTICE file in a
    repository does not automatically reach the recipient of a built artifact.
    Every build therefore carries `licenses/primus/` — the LGPL-3.0 text taken
    from the pinned submodule itself, the GPL-3.0 text it incorporates by
    reference, and `PRIMUS.txt` recording the fork URL, the built commit, and
    step-by-step instructions for rebuilding or replacing the Primus portion.
    See `licenses/README.md` and `primusLicenseAssets()` in `modules/primus.ts`.

  * **The modifications.** `modules/primus.ts` in this repository is the complete
    set of build-time patches applied to that source.

  * **The right to modify and relink.** `LICENSE` expressly preserves the right
    to modify the LGPL portion, reverse engineer for debugging those changes,
    and recombine or relink a locally built Extension with that modified portion.


Bundled fonts
-------------

The extension registers web fonts at runtime from bytes baked into the bundle at
build time (see `src/signal/load-fonts.ts`). Each is distributed under the SIL
Open Font License 1.1:

  - Inter        — https://github.com/rsms/inter
  - Geist Mono   — https://github.com/vercel/geist-font

Other dependencies
------------------

Remaining runtime and build dependencies are declared in `package.json` and
resolved by `pnpm-lock.yaml`. Before public distribution, generate and review a
complete dependency licence inventory and add any required notices or licence
texts to the distributed artifact; this repository does not yet claim that work
is complete.
